# Gateway Rules

Local OpenAI-compatible HTTP server on **`127.0.0.1` only** (default port 4001).
Public reachability is via tunnel / BYO URL — see `tunnel.mdc`.

## Key model (upstream ×2 + gateway)

|| Key                       | Config field           | Who sees it                          ||
|| ------------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------ ||
|| Moonshot / Kimi API key   | `moonshotKeyEncrypted` | App only → Authorization to Moonshot ||
|| DeepSeek API key          | `deepseekKeyEncrypted` | App only → Authorization to DeepSeek ||
|| Thaura AI API key         | `thauraKeyEncrypted`   | App only → Authorization to Thaura   ||
|| Z.AI API key              | `zaiKeyEncrypted`      | App only → Authorization to Z.AI      ||
|| Gateway key (`sk-{alnum}`) | `gatewayKey`           | Cursor as "OpenAI API Key"           ||

Never log or return upstream provider keys. Wrong gateway key → OpenAI-shaped 401.
Routing picks which upstream key to use from the **model map** (alias → provider).

### Upstream base URLs (code SoT)

Hardcoded defaults + optional env overrides live in
`internal/config/urls.go` (`UpstreamBaseURL`, `ChatCompletionsURL`).

|| Provider | Default base                 ||
|| -------- | ---------------------------- ||
|| moonshot | `https://api.moonshot.ai/v1` ||
|| deepseek | `https://api.deepseek.com`   ||
|| openrouter | `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1` ||
|| thaura   | `https://backend.thaura.ai/v1` ||
|| zai       | `https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4` ||

Use those helpers so Moonshot's `/v1` and DeepSeek's host root never produce
`/v1/v1/...`. Do not scatter raw URL string literals in the gateway proxy.

## Endpoints (MVP)

|| Endpoint                    | Purpose                                              ||
|| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- ||
|| `GET /health`               | Status, metrics, URLs, which provider keys present   ||
|| `GET|POST /v1/models`      | Advertise aliases + real ids (+ provider)            ||
|| `POST /v1/chat/completions` | Main path                                            ||
|| `POST /v1/responses`        | Same handler after Responses→Chat adapt              ||
|| Other `/v1/*`               | Proxy when cheap (embeddings/files) — provider-aware ||

## Model map (alias → provider → real id)

Switching providers/models for the user is **choosing the Cursor alias** (or a
listed real id). One table drives sanitize policy, upstream base URL, API key,
and pricing row.

### Primary Cursor aliases (Agent-first)

|| Cursor alias    | Provider | Real model       | Typical use         ||
|| --------------- | -------- | ---------------- | ------------------- ||
|| `gpt-4o`        | moonshot | `kimi-k3`         | Planning / flagship ||
|| `gpt-4o-mini`   | moonshot | `kimi-k2.7-code`  | Coding; always thinks ||
|| `o1`            | deepseek | `deepseek-v4-pro` | Harder execution    ||
|| `o3-mini`       | deepseek | `deepseek-v4-flash` | Cheap execution     ||
|| `gpt-5-nano`    | thaura   | `thaura`          | Ethical AI; optional provider ||
|| `gpt-4.1-turbo` | zai      | `glm-5.3[1m]`    | 1M context flagship; always thinks ||
|| `gpt-4.1`       | zai      | `glm-4.7`         | Budget workhorse; thinking on/off ||
|| `gpt-4-turbo`   | zai      | `glm-5.3[1m]`    | **Compat alias** — Cursor rewrites `gpt-4.1-turbo` → `gpt-4-turbo` ||

> **Peak-hour OpenRouter reroute (always on, HARD RULE: OpenRouter is peak-only).**
> During DeepSeek peak (01:00–04:00, 06:00–10:00 UTC Beijing weekdays) or Z.AI
> peak (Mon–Fri 06:00–10:00 UTC) `applyPeakReroute` (`peakguard.go`) swaps to
> each provider's OpenRouter twin from `config.OpenRouterTwinFor` (`providers.go`):
> DeepSeek flash/pro → `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731` /
> `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813`; Z.AI glm-5.3/glm-4.7 → `z-ai/glm-5.3` /
> `z-ai/glm-4.7`. Moonshot/Thaura never peak. **Outside peak hours OpenRouter is
> never used.** Subagent/router downgrades use the **same provider's small model**
> (`config.SmallModelFor`) — never cross-provider. Send-time guard:
> `isPeakAllowedOpenRouter`; `DISCURSIVE_FORCE_PEAK` simulates peak. No OR key?
> Peak traffic falls through to the direct provider and pays peak rates. Logs
> `peak_reroute` at INFO with from/to + request_id. Applies to non-downgraded
> traffic only.

Set the alias manually in Cursor Settings → Models. The gateway maps it and
picks the right base URL + API key. No auto-application to Cursor's state.vscdb
— operators configure Cursor by hand (see `cursor-settings.mdc`).

### `Cursor rewrites a model ID (model picker ≠ sent model)`

|| Symptom | Cause | Fix ||
|| ------- | ----- | ---- ||
|| Model picker shows `gpt-4.1-turbo`, but the gateway logs `unknown model alias "gpt-4-turbo"` | Cursor performs its own client-side model-ID matching against its internal OpenAI catalog and may substitute a close/known ID (drops the `.1`) before sending | (1) Advertise the real IDs in `/v1/models`; (2) accept the rewritten ID as a **compat alias** mapping to the same real model (`gpt-4-turbo` → `glm-5.3[1m]`). Do not treat the rewritten name as a gateway bug. ||

## Sanitizer order (preserve)

1. Map Cursor alias → **{provider, real model}** (table above)
2. Apply **provider- and model-aware** thinking / sampling policy
   (`kimi.mdc` or `deepseek.mdc` or `zai.mdc`)
3. Map `max_completion_tokens` → `max_tokens`; clamp per model context
4. Strip incompatible OpenAI/Cursor sampling fields
5. Adapt Responses `input`/`instructions` → `messages`
6. Repair tool_call ids / pairing; sanitize tool names + JSON Schema
7. Seed empty probe message when tools present and messages empty
8. Message role fixes (`developer`→`system`); reasoning placeholder for tool-call assistants when required

Then proxy to the resolved provider base URL with that provider's key. Stream
what Cursor asked for (passthrough SSE or synthesize). Retry once on upstream
400s mentioning `tool_call_id` (when that provider returns them).

Behavioral checklist: refer to provider-specific rules (`.cursor/rules/kimi.mdc`,
`.cursor/rules/deepseek.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/thaura.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/zai.mdc`) for
model-specific quirks.

## Hard routing (no cross-provider fallback)

> **2026-08 refactor.** The gateway never switches providers on the same request
> path. Peak reroute is an OpenRouter **transport swap** to the same model's OR
> twin only. Subagent router: `config.SmallModelFor(provider)`. Compressor and
> vision use the request provider's small/vision models; OR twin on peak for the
> compressor when that provider peaks.

|| Symptom | Cause | Fix ||
|| ------- | ----- | ---- ||
|| Z.AI returns HTTP 429 (overloaded / insufficient balance) for `glm-5.3`/`glm-4.7` | Plan concurrency or quota blip; no cross-provider escape hatch. | `doUpstreamWithRetry()` in `proxy.go`: up to **3** retries with exponential backoff (250ms → 500ms → 1s). Return 429 to Cursor after retries exhaust. ||
|| GLM turns slow when many concurrent subagents hit Z.AI | Coding-plan concurrency ~2 upstream; requests queue or 429. | No gateway overflow to other providers. Subagent router downgrades within Z.AI to `glm-4.7`. Reduce parallel Z.AI load; expect 429 retries. ||

### Historical — pre-2026-08 semaphore overflow (superseded)

|| Symptom | Cause | Fix (historical) ||
|| ------- | ----- | ---- ||
|| Z.AI 429 under heavy load | `zaiSem` overflow to DeepSeek | **Removed.** Hard routing + `doUpstreamWithRetry` replaced `zaiSem`/`acquireZaiLaneOrOverflow`/`selectDowngradeLane`. ||
|| glm-4.6v starved chat budget | Separate vision semaphore | Vision now uses `config.VisionModelFor(provider)` per provider; no shared `zaiSem`. ||
|| Direct glm-4.7 hung 20-45s when plan slots busy | `acquireZaiSlot` blocked instead of overflowing | **Removed with semaphore model.** ||
|| Cannot verify lane overflow | No `glm47LaneInUse` counter | **Removed with semaphore.** Use `peak_reroute` + `subagent_router` logs instead. ||

