## Retry logic (transient Z.AI errors)

|| Symptom | Cause | Fix ||
|| ------- | ----- | ---- ||
|| Z.AI request fails with HTTP 429, succeeds on retry | Transient plan/concurrency blip. | `doUpstreamWithRetry()` for all Z.AI chat: on HTTP 429, retry up to **3** times with exponential backoff (250ms → 500ms → 1s). Return the 429 to Cursor only after retries exhaust. Non-Z.AI providers call `doUpstream()` directly. ||

## Tool-result compression tuning

|| Symptom | Cause | Fix ||
|| ------- | ----- | ---- ||
|| Compression fires on small tool results, paying 1-3s latency + flash cost for minimal token savings | Threshold too low (4000 chars); no token-budget awareness; empty-summary failures paid full cost then sent original | Raise `toolResultMaxLen` to 24000; add `compressMinTotalChars` (20000 chars aggregate gate); truncate on summarizer failure instead of fail-open; detect soft failures (empty/not-shorter) to truncate per-job without aborting batch ||

