## Terseness (always on)

- Purpose: coerce models to be terse (code-first, prose-light) during agentic loops.
- **Always on** — no dashboard toggle, no `GET/PUT /api/verbosity` (removed 2026-08).
- Implemented in `internal/gateway/verbosity/`; applied in `proxy.go` after routing.
- Three request-side mechanisms — **never edits response content**:
  1. **Directive injection** — appends terseness directive to last system/developer message
  2. **Token cap** — lowers `max_tokens` per model (`deepseek-v4-flash` 4096, `deepseek-v4-pro` 8192, `glm-4.7` 8192, `glm-5.3` 16384)
- Terseness applies **after** subagent-router downgrade so the final served model determines caps

## Runtime settings (no restart)

|| Aspect | Detail ||
|| ------- | ------ ||
|| Compression runtime toggles | `GET/PUT /api/settings` in usage UI → applies immediately, no restart ||
|| Config fields | `ToolCompressionEnabled bool`, `ThinkingEnabled map[string]bool` (in `AppSettings`/`LiveSettings`) ||
|| Tool threshold | `toolResultMaxLen` (24000 chars); `compressMinTotalChars` (20000 aggregate gate) ||
|| Failure / key-missing | Soft failures (empty/not-shorter summary) truncate to `toolResultMaxLen`; hard errors fail-open with original body ||

